hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said regarding the sea,\n\"It's water is purifying and its dead (animals) are lawful (to eat).\" \n\n[Al- Arba’a and Ibn Abu Shaiba reported it (this version is of the latter). Ibn Khuzaima and Tirmidhi graded it Sahih. It was also reported by Malik, Shafi'i and Ahmad.]"
"2","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said: “Water is pure and nothing can make it impure”.\n\n[Ath-Thalatha and Ahmad who graded it Sahih]"
"3","Narrated Abu Umama Al-Bahili:\nAllah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said: “Water cannot be rendered impure by anything except something which changes its smell, taste and colour”. \n[ Ibn Majar reported it and Abu Hatim described it as Da’if (weak)]."
"4","“Water is pure unless any impure thing is added which changes its smell, taste and colour”."
"5","Allah’s Mesenger (ﷺ) said:\n“If there is enough water to fill two pots (Qulla), it carries no impurity,” Another version has: “It does not become unclean”.\n{Al-Arba’a reported it. Ibn Khuzaima, Ibn Hibban and Al-Hakim graded it Sahih (sound)]."
"6","Narrated Abu Huraira (rad):\nAllah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said:\n“None of you should take a bath in stagnant water when he is sexually impure”. [Muslim reported it]"
"7","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) forbade a women to bathe with the water left over by a man and that a man should not bathe with the water left over by a woman (but instead) they should both take scoopfuls of the water together. [Reported by Abu Da’ud and An-Nasa’i and its chain of narrators is Sahih (authentic)]."
"8","Narrated Ibn ‘Abbas (rad):\nThe Prophet (ﷺ) used to bath with the water left over by Maimuna (rad) [Muslim reported it]."
"9","And Ashab As-Sunan (compilers of the prophet’s sayings) reported that one of the wives of the Prophet (ﷺ) took bath from a vessel, then came the Prophet (ﷺ) and when he wanted to take bath from that (vessel), she said, “I was sexually impure”. He said, “Water does not become sexually impure”. [At-Tirmidhi and Ibn huzaima graded it Sahih (sound)]."
"10","Narrated by Abu Huraira (rad):\nAllah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said: “The cleansing of the utensil belonging to one of you, after it has been licked by a dog, is to wash it seven times, and using soil for cleaning at the first time.” [Muslim reported it]."
"11","Narrated Abu Qatada (rad):\nAllah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said about the cat that, “It is not unclean, but is one of those who intermingle with you.” [Reported by Al-Arba’a. At-Tirmidhi and Ibn Khuzaima graded it Sahih (sound)]."
"12","Narrated Anas bin Malik (rad): \nA Bedouin came and urinated in one corner of the mosque and the people shouted at him, but Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) stopped them, and when he finished urinating, the Prophet (ﷺ) ordered for a bucket of water which was spilt over it [Agreed upon]."
"13","Narrated Ibn 'Umar (rad): \nAllah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said: \"Two types of dead animals and two types of bloods have been made lawful for us, the two types of dead animals are locusts and fish (seafood), while the two types of bloods are the liver and the spleen\". [Reported by Ahmad and Ibn Majah, and this Hadith has some weakness.]"
"14","Narrated Abu Huraira (rad):\nAllah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said: “When a fly falls in the drink of one of you, he should fully dip it and then throw it away because there is disease in one of its wings and cure in the other”. [Reported by Al-Bukhari]"
"15","Narrated Abu Waqid Al-Laithi (rad):\nAllah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said: “Whatever (portion) is cut off from an animal when it is alive is dead (meat). [Reported by Abu Da’ud and At-Tirmidhi who graded it Hasan (fair) and this version is of Tirmidhi]."
"16","Narrated Hudhaifa bin Al-Yaman (rad):\nAllah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said: “Do not drink in silver or gold utensils, and do not eat in plates of such metals, for such things are for them (the disbelievers) in this worldly life and for you in the Hereafter.” [Agreed upon]"
"17","Narrated Umm Salama (rad):\nAllah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said: “He who drinks in a silver utensil is only swallowing Hell-fire in his stomach”. [Agreed Upon]"
"18","Narrated (rad):\nAllah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said: \"When the skin is tanned it becomes purified.” [Reported by Muslim]. Al-Arba’a have the words: \"Any skin that is tanned ... \""
"19","Narrated (rad):\nAllah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said: “The tanning of a dead animal’s skin purifies it”. [Ibn Hibban graded it Sahih (sound)]."
"20","Narrated (rad):\nSome people dragging a (dead) goat passed by the Prophet (ﷺ). He told them, “Had you better taken its skin”. They said, “It is dead”. He said, “Water and the leaves of the Acacia tree will purify it”. [Reported by Abu Da’ud and An’Nasa’i]."
"21","Narrated (rad):\nI said “O Allah’s Messenger! We are living in a land inhabited by the people of the Scriptures; can we take our meals in their utensils?” He said, “If you can get utensils other than theirs, do not eat in theirs, but if you cannot get other than theirs, wash them and eat in them” [Agreed upon]."
"22","The Prophet (ﷺ) and his Companions performed Wudu (ablution) from a skin water container belonging to a polytheist woman [Agreed upon]. (It is an extract of a long Hadith)."
"23","Narrated Anas bin Malik (rad):\nWhen the cup of the Prophet (ﷺ) got broken, he fixed it with a silver wire at the crack [Reported by Al-Bukhari]."
"24","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) was asked about making vinegar out of wine. He said, “No (it is prohibited)”. [Reported by Muslim, and At-Tirmidhi and the latter graded it Hasan-Sahih (fair and sound)]."
"25","On the day of Khaibair, Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) commanded Abu Talha to announce: “Allah and His Messenger have prohibited for you (eating of) the flesh of the donkeys, for it is unclean”. [Agreed upon]."
"26","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) delivered a Khutba (religious talk) to us at Mina while mounted on his camel and its saliva was pouring on my shoulders [Reported by Ahmad and At-Trimidhi and the latter graded it Sahih (sound)]."
"27","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) used to wash the semen and then go out for prayer in that (very) garment and I could still see the trace of the washing on it. [Agreed upon]"
"28","“I used to scrape it (the semen) off the garment of Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) and then he offered prayer with it."
"29","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said: “The urine of a baby girl should be washed off and the urine of baby boy should be sprinkled (with water)”. [Reported by Abu Da’ud and An-Nasa’i and Al-Hakim graded it Sahih (sound)]."
"30","The Prophet (Saw) said regarding menstruation blood that smears a garment, “She should scrape it, rub it with water, then wash it and then she may pray in it”. [Agreed upon]"
"31","Khaula said, “O Messenger of Allah, suppose the (trace of) the blood does not go?” He said, “(Washing it with) water will suffice you and its trace won’t harm you”. [Reported by At Tirmidhi, and its Sanad (chain of narrators) is weak]."
"32","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said “Had I not feared burdening my Ummah, I would have commanded them to use Siwak with every ablution.” [Reported by Malik, Ahmad and An-Nasai. Ibn Khuzaima graded it Sahih (sound) and Al-Bukhari mentioned as a Mu’allaq (suspended – without its chain of narrators)."
"33","Uthman (rad) called for water to perform ablution. He washed palms of his hands three times, then rinsed his mouth and sniffed water in his nose and then blew it out. He then washed his face three times. Thereafter he washed his right hand up to his elbow three times, then the left one likewise, then he passed wet hands on his head. Then he washed his right foot up to the ankle three times, then the left one likewise. He then said, “I saw Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) performing ablution like this ablution of mine”. [Agreed upon]"
"34","He (the Prophet) wiped his head (with water) only once. [Reported by Abu Da’ud, An-Nasa’i, AtTirmidhi with a Sahih Sanad (authentic chain of narrators). At-Tirmidhi said, “It’s the most Hadith on this subject”]."
"35","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) wiped his head from the forehead to the back of his head and then back to the forehead with his (wet) hands. [ Agreed upon ]."
"36","“Then he (Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ)) wiped his head, inserted his index finger in his ears and wiped the exterior of his ears with thumbs”. [Reported by Abu Da’ud and An-Nasa’i and Ibn Khuzaima graded it Sahih (sound)]."
"37","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said: “When one of you wakes up from his sleep, he must blow of his nose three times, for the Satan spends the night inside one’s nostrils” [Agreed upon]."
"38","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said: “When one of you wakes up from his sleep, he must not put his hand in a utensil till he washed it three times, for he does not know where his hand was (while he slept)”.\n[Agreed upon. This is Muslim’s version]."
"39","Allah’s Mesenger (ﷺ) said: “Perform a perfect Wudu run (your fingers) through the fingers of the hands and the toes, and if not fasting, sniff water up well inside the nose”. [Reported by Al-Arba’a and Ibn Khuzaima graded it Sahih]."
"40","While performing Wudu, the Prophet (ﷺ) would run (his fingers) through his beard. [Reported by At-Tirmidhi and Ibn Khuzaima graded it Sahih]."
"41","Two thirds of a Mudd (of water) was brought to he Prophet (ﷺ) (for ablution) so he began rubbing his arms. [Reported by Ahmed, and Ibn Khuzaima graded it Sahih]."
"42","He saw the Prophet (ﷺ) taking some water to wipe his ears other than the water he had taken to wipe his head. [Reported by Al-Baihaqi, who said that its Isnad (chain of narrators) is authentic and At-Tirmidhi also graded it Sahih]."
"43","I heard Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) saying, “My people will come on the Day of Resurrection with bright faces, hands and feet from the traces of Wudu. If any of you can lengthen his brightness, let him do so”. [Agreed upon and this is Muslim’s version]."
"44","Allah’s Messenger (rad) loved to begin with the right while putting on his shoes, combing his hair, in his purification and in all his affairs [Agreed upon]."
"45","Allah’s Messenger (rad) said: “When you perform ablution, begin with your right limbs”. [Reported by Al-Arba’a and garded Sahih by Ibn Khuzaima]."
"46","The Prophet (ﷺ) performed ablution and passed wet hands on his forelock, over the turban and over the two leather socks. [ Reported by Muslim]."
"47","Regarding the Hajj of the Prophet (ﷺ): He said, “Begin with what Allah had begun with” [ Reported by An-Nasa’i in this commanding version while Muslim has reported it in the reporting one]."
"48","The Prophet (ﷺ) used to run the water down his elbows while performing ablution [Reported by Ad-Daraqutni with aweak chain of narrators]."
"49","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said: “There is no Wudu for one who does not mention Allah’s Name upon it. [Reported by Ahmad, Abu Da’ud and Ibn Majah with a weak chain of narrators]."
"50","At-Tirmidhi reported something similar to the above from Sa’id bin Zaid."
"51","And from him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, used to perform ablution with a Mudd and perform Ghusl with a Sa' up to five Mudd. Agreed upon."
"52","“I saw Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) rinsing his mouth and sniffing up and blowing his nose with separate scops of water.” [Reported by Abu Da’ud with a weak chain of narrators]."
"53","The Prophet (ﷺ) rinsed his mouth and sniffed and blew (his nose) with water three times. He sniffed up and blew his nose with the same hand from which he took the water. [Reported by Abu Da’ud and An-Nasa’i]"
"54","The Prophet (ﷺ) put his hand (in the utensil) rinsed (his mouth) and sniffed up and blew (his nose) from one scoop (of water). He did that three times. [Agreed upon]."
"55","The Prophet (ﷺ) saw a man on whose foot appeared a portion like the size of a nail which was not touched by water. He then said, “Go back and perform your Wudu properly.” [Reported by Abu Da’ud and An-Nasa’i]."
"56","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) used only one Mudd of water for ablution and one Sa’ to five Mudd of water for his bath [ Agreed upon]."
"57","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said: “If one after performing ablution completely recites the following supplication: (Ash-hadu an la ilaha ill-Allahu wahdahu la sharika lahu, wa ash hadu anna Muhammadan ‘abduhu wa Rasuluhu) ‘I testify that there is no one worthy of worship but Allah, He is Alone and has no partner and Muhammad (ﷺ) is his slave and Messenger’, all the eight gates of Paradise will be opened for him and he may enter through any gate he wishes”."
"58","Once I was in the company of the Prophet (ﷺ), he then performed ablution and I dashed to take off his socks. He said, “Leave them for I had put them on after performing ablution”. So he wiped over them [Agreed Upon]."
"59","The Prophet (ﷺ) wiped over the upper part of the leather socks and the under part of it.\n[In its chain of narrators there is weakness]."
"60","If the religion were based on opinion, it would be more important to wipe over the under parts of the leather socks than the upper, but I have seen Allah’s Messenger (rad) wiping over the upper parts of his leather socks. [Reported by Abu Da’ud with good Isnad (chain of narrators)]."
"61","When we were on a journey, the Prophet (ﷺ) used to command us to wear our leather socks for three days and three nights, whether we had to answer the call of nature or slept. However, in case of ejaculation or sexual impurity, he commanded us to remove the leather socks. [Reported by An-Nasa’i and At-Tirmidhi, version is of the latter. With them Ibn Khuzaima graded it Sahih (sound)]."
"62","The Prophet (ﷺ) fixed the period of Mash (wiping) over the leather socks (Khifaf – plural of Khuff) for three days and nights for a traveller and one day and a night for the resident person in a town [Reported by Muslim]."
"63","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) sent out a military expedition and commanded them to wipe over the turbans and leather socks. [ Reported by Ahmad and Abu Da’ud. Al-Hakim graded it Sahih (sound)]."
"64","“If one of you performs ablution and puts on his two leather socks, let him perform Mash (wipe) over them and pray in them and he may not take them off he so wishes except after ejaculation or sexual impurity. [Reported by Ad-Daraqutni and Al-Hakim and graded Sahih (sound) by him]."
"65","The Prophet (ﷺ) gave permission for the traveller to perform Mash (wiping) over his leather socks for three days and nights and for a non-traveller for a day and night, if he had put them on in a state of purity. [Reported by Ad-Daraqutni and graded Sahih (sound) by Ibnn Khuzaima]."
"66","I asked, “O Messenger of Allah, may I wipe over the Khuffain (leather socks)?” The Prophet (ﷺ) replied, “Yes”. I asked, “For one day?” He replied, “For one day”, I again asked, “And for two days?” He replied “For two day s too”. I again asked “And for three days” He replied, “Yes, as long as you wish”. [Reported by Abu Da’ud, who said, “It is not strong”]"
"67","The Companions of Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) in his lifetime used to wait for the ‘Isha (night) prayer, so much so that their heads were lowered down (by dozing). They would then pray without performing ablution. [Reported by Abu Da’ud and Ad-Daraqutni graded it Sahih (sound). Its origin is in Muslim]."
"68","Fatima bint Abu Hubaish came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I am a woman whose blood keeps flowing (even after the menstruation). I am never purified; should I, therefore, stop praying?” He (the Prophet) said: “No, for that is only a vein, and is not menstruation. So when the menstruation comes, abstain from prayers, and when it ends wash the blood from yourself and then pray”. [Agreed upon]."
"69","I was one who Madhi (urethral discharge) flowed readily and asked Miqdad (his slave) to ask the Prophet (ﷺ) about it. He (the Prophet) said:“One should perform Wudu (ablution) in this case”. [Agreed upon and this is Al-Bukhari’s version]."
"70","The Prophet (ﷺ) kissed one of his wives and went to pray without performing (fresh) ablution. [Reported by Ahmad and Al-Bukhari graded it Da’if (weak)]."
"71","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said: “If one of you feels disturbance in his stomach and doubts whether he has released some wind or not, then he should not leave the mosque unless he hears its sound or smells (its) odour”. [Reported by Muslim]."
"72","A man said: “I touched my penis” or he said, “Does a man who touch his penis during the prayer should perform Wudu (ablution)?” The Prophet (ﷺ) replied, “No, it is only a part of your body”. [Reported by Al-Khamsa. Ibn Hibban graded it Sahih (sound)."
"73","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said: “He who touches his penis should perform ablution”. [Reported by Al-Khamsa, and At-Tirmidhi and Ibn Hibban graded it Sahih (sound)."
"74","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said: “Whoever vomits, bleeds through the nose, or released Madhi (urethral discharge) should go, perform ablution and then complete his Salat (prayer) (by continuing from where he had stopped at) on condition that he does not speak in the process”. \nReported by Ibn Majah"
"75","A man asked the Prophet (ﷺ), “Should I perform ablution after eating mutton?” He replied, “If you wish so”, he then asked, “Should I perform ablution after eating camel meat?” He (ﷺ) said: “Yes”.\n[Reported by Muslim]."
"76","The Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Whoever washes a dead person should take a bath (thereafter); and whoever carries it should perform ablution”. Reported by Ahmad, An-Nasa’i and At-Tirmidhi who graded it Hasan (fair)."
"77","The book written by Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) for ‘Amr bin Hazm also contained: “ None except a pure person should touch the Quran”. [Reported by Malik as a Mursal and by An-Nasa’i and Ibn Hibban as Mawsul. And it is graded as Ma’lul (defective)]."
"78","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) used to mention Allah’s Name (praise Him) at all times.\n[Reported by Muslim and Al-Bukhari recorded it as Mu’allaq (suspended)]."
"79","The Prophet (ﷺ) had blood extracted from his body and offered the prayer and did not perform (a new) ablution. [Reported by Ad-Daraqutni who graded it Da’if (weak)]."
"80","Allah’s Messenger (saW) said: “The eye (when awake) is the string of the anus (to stop air escaping), and if the two eyes sleep the string is untied”. [Reported by Ahmad and At-Tabarani who added, “Whoever sleeps should perform ablution]”"
"81","Also reported by Abu Da’ud mentioning the above addition without the words “the string is untied”, but both versions are weak."
"82","“Ablution is necessary for one who sleeps while he is lying flat. [Reported by Abu Da’ud and there is weakness in its chain of narrators]."
"83","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said: “Satan comes to one of you in Salat and blows air in his bottom, so he imagines that he has realised air yet he did not. So if he gets that feeling he should not leave his prayer unless he hears the sound (of the air) or smells its odour.” [Reported by Al-Bazzar]."
"84","It is originally from the Sahihain of Bukhari and Muslim as the Hadith narrated by ‘Abdullah bin Zaid."
"85","And for the Seven (Imams) from the narration of Abu Ayyub, may Allah be pleased with him: \"Do not face the Qiblah with excrement or urine, nor turn your backs to it, but rather face east or west.\""
"86","“If Satan comes to one of you and says: ‘You have nullified your ablution (by releasing air)’, let him say: ‘You have lied.” [Reported by Al-Hakim]."
"87","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) used to remove his ring when entering the lavatory. [Reported by Al-Arba’a and it is defective]."
"88","The Prophet (ﷺ) on entering the lavatory used to say: \n[Allahumma inni a’udhu bika minal khubthi wal khaba’ithi]\n“O Allah, I seek refuge with You from devils – males and females (or all offensive and wicked things, evil deeds and evil spirits, etc.)” [Reported by As-Sab’a]"
"89","Whenever Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) went to the privy, a servant and I used to carry a skin water container and a spear, and he would cleanse himself with the water. [Agreed upon]."
"90","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) told me, “Take the skin water”, he then went forward till he disappeared from me and relieved himself [Agreed upon]"
"91","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said: “Safeguard yourselves from the two matters which cause accursing that befalls the one who relieves himself on people’s path-ways and under the shades.” [Reported by Muslim]."
"92","He said: “Guard against the three things which cause curse (i.e.) defecating at the watering places, on the roadbeds and in the shades.” [Reported by Abu Dawud]"
"93","Ahmad reported from Ibn Abbas (rad) that defecation is prohibited also at the place where water collects. [And both the two (i.e. the previous and this Hadiths) have weakness]."
"94","At-Tabarani also narrated on the authority of Ibn ‘Umar (with a weak chain of narrators), the prohibition of relieving oneself under fruit trees and beside the bank of a flowing river."
"95","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said: “When two people go together to relieve themselves they should disappear from each other and do not talk, for Allah detests that”. [Reported by Ahmad; Ibn As-Sakan and Ibn Al-Qattan graded it Sahih (sound) but it is defective]."
"96","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said: “Nobody should touch his pennies with his right hand when urinating, and should not clean himself (from defecation or urine) using his right hand and should not breathe in the utensil (he is drinking from).” [Agreed upon. This version is of Muslim]."
"97","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) forbade us to face the Qiblah when defecating or urinating, or to clean ourselves using the right hand, or to clean ourselves with less than three stones, or to clean ourselves with dung or a bone [Reported by Muslim]."
"98","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) “Neither face nor turn your back to the Qiblah while defecating or urinating, but turn towards the east or the west”. [Reported by the As-Sab’a]"
"99","The Prophet (ﷺ) said: “If anyone goes to relive himself, he should conceal himself”. [Reported by Abu Da’ud]."
"100","When the Prophet (ﷺ) came out of the privy, he used to say, “Ghufranaka (O Allah! Grant me Your forgiveness)”. [Reported by Al-Khamsa, Abu Hatim and Al-Hakim graded it Sahih (sound)]."
"101","The Prophet (ﷺ) went out to answer the call of nature and asked me to bring three stones. I found two stones and searched for the third but could not find it. So I took a dried piece of dung and brought it to him. He took the two stones and threw away the dung and said, “This is a filthy thing”. [Reported by Al-Bukhari]"
"102","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) forbade us to use a bone or dung for cleaning and said, “These two things do not purify”. [Reported by Ad-Daraqutni who graded it Sahih]."
"103","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said: “Beware of (smearing yourselves with) urine, because it is the main cause of punishment in the grave”. [Reported by Ad-Daraqutni]"
"104","“Urination is the main cause of punishment in the grave”. [Its chain of narrators is authentic]."
"105","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) educated us about lavatory (manners) that we should sit on our left foot and keep erect our right foot. [Reported by Al-Baihaqi through a chain of weak narrators]."
"106","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said: “When one of you passes urine, he should empty his penis three times”. [Reported by Ibn Majah through a weak chain of narrators]."
"107","The Prophet (ﷺ) asked the residents of Quba that what had earned them the Praise of Allah and they replied, “We use water after (cleaning ourselves with) stones.” [Reported by Al-Bazzar with Da’if chain of narrators]"
"108","and its Asl (original source) is in Abu Da’ud and At-Tirmidhi and Ibn Khuzaima graded it Sahih (sound) through Abu Huraira (rad) without mentioning the “stones”.]"
"109","Allah’s Mesenger (ﷺ) said: “The water (of the ghusl) is due to the water (of sexual emission)”. [Reported by Muslim]"
"110","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said that, “If one of you sits between her legs (of a woman) and penetrates her, Ghusl (bath) is obligatory.” [Agreed upon]."
"111","Umm Sulaim, the wife Abu Talha said, “O Allah’s Messenger! Allah is not ashamed of the truth. Is a Ghusl (bath) compulsory for a woman when she has a sexual dream?” He (ﷺ) replied, “Yes! When she sees signs of liquid” [Agreed upon]."
"112","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) used to take a bath from four things; after sexual intercourse, on Fridays, after extracting blood from his body and after washing a dead body. [Reported by Abu Da’ud and Ibn Khuzaima graded it Sahih (sound)]"
"113","The Prophet (ﷺ) ordered him to take a bath. [Narrated by Abdur-Razzaq]"
"114","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said: “Taking a bath on Friday is a must for every adult”. [Reported by As-Sab’a]."
"115","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said: “Whoever performs ablution on Friday has done a good thing and he who takes bath, taking bath is better (for him).” [Reported by Al-Khamsa and At-Tirmidhi graded it Hasan (fair).]"
"116","The Prophet (ﷺ) used to teach us the Qur’an except when he was in a state of sexual impurity. [Reported by Ahmad and Al-Arba’a. This is the version of At-Tirmidhi who graded it Hasan (fair). And Ibn Hibban graded it Sahih (sound)]."
"117","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said: “If one of you has sexual intercourse with his wife and wishes to repeat he should perform ablution between them” [Reported by Muslim]."
"118","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) used to sleep in the state of sexual impurity without touching water. [Reported by Al-Arba’a. This Hadith is defective]."
"119","Whenever Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) took Ghusl (bath) after sexual intercourse, he would begin by washing his hands, then pour water with his right hand on his left hand and wash his sexual organ. He would then perform ablution, then take some water and run his fingers through the roots of the hair. Then he would pour three handfuls on his head, then pour water over the rest of his body and subsequently wash his feet. [Agreed upon and this version is of Muslim]"
"120","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) poured water over his private parts and washed them with his left hand. He then struck his hand against the earth."
"121","I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I am a woman who keeps her hair closely plaited. Do I have to undo them for Ghusl after sexual intercourse?\" In another narration, \"and after the end of menses?\" He replied (ﷺ), \"No, is it enough for you to throw three handfuls of water over your head.\"\nRelated by Muslim."
"122","Allah's messenger (ﷺ) said: \"It is not permitted for a menstruating woman or one who is junub (sexually impure) to stay in the mosque.\"\nRelated by Abu Dawud and Ibn Khuzaimah graded it as Sahih"
"123","I and Allah's Messenger (Peace be upon him) took a Ghusl (bath) due to sexual impurity from the same vessel and our hands alternated into it.\n[Agreed upon.]\n\nIbn Hibban added \"and (our hands) met.\""
"124","Allah's Messenger (Peace be upon him) said: \"There is Janabah (trace of sexual impurity) under every hair, so wash your hair and cleanse the skin.\"\nAbu Dawud and at-Tirmidhi transmitted it but they declared it to be weak."
"125","Ahmad transmitted a similar narration to the above, on the authority of `A'ishah (RAA), but this version has an unknown transmitter."
"126","The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"I have been given five things which were not given to anyone else before me. Allah made me victorious by awe (of frightening my enemies) for a distance of one month's journey. The earth has been made for me (and my followers) a place for praying and something with which to perform Tayammum (to purify oneself for prayer). Therefore, anyone (of my followers) can pray (anywhere) and at any time that the Salat (prayer) is due.\""
"127","\"And the soil of the earth had been made for us as a means with which to purify ourselves (for prayer), when we cannot find water.\"\nRelated by Muslim."
"128","\"The earth (dust) has been made for me as a means for purification.\""
"129","The Prophet (ﷺ) sent me on some errands and I became junub (sexually impure), and could not find water. I rolled myself in the dirt just as an animal does. I then came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and mentioned that to him. He said, \"This would have been enough for you,\" and he struck the earth with his hands once, then he wiped the right hand with the left one, and the outside of the palms of his hands and his face.\n[Agreed upon. The wording is that of Muslim's]."
"130","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said: \"Tayammum is two strikes: one for the face and one for the hands up to the elbows.\"\nReported by Ad-Daraqutni"
"131","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said: \"The soil is a purifier for a Muslim, even if he does not find water for ten years; but if he finds water, he must fear Allah and let it touch his skin.\""
"132","Narrated Abu Dharr (RAA):a similar Hadith transmitted by at-Tirmidhi وَلِلتِّرْمِذِيِّ: عَنْ أَبِي ذَرٍّ نَحْوُهُ, وَصَحَّحَه ُ 1 .1 - صحيح. رواه الترمذي (124) ولفظه: \"إن الصعيد الطيب طهور المسلم، وإن لم يجد الماء عشر سنين، فإذا وجد الماء فليمسه بشرته؛ فإن ذلك خير\" وقال: \"حديث حسن صحيح\"."
"133","Two men set out on a journey and when the time of Salat (prayer) came they had no water. They performed Tayammum with clean earth and prayed. Later on they found water within the time of the prayer. One of them repeated his prayer with ablution but the other did not repeat. Then they came to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ), and related the matter to him. Addressing himself to the one who did not repeat, he said, \"You followed the Sunnah and your (first) prayer was enough for you.\"[9] He said to the one who performed ablution and repeated: \"For you there is a double reward\".\n[Reported by Abu Dawud and An-Nasa'i]"
"134","concerning the verse, “And if you are ill or on a journey...” (an-Nisa': 43). He said, \"If a man sustains a wound, which he suffered during Jihad (in the cause of Allah) or ulcers, then he became junub (sexually impure) and is afraid that if he bathes he would die; he may perform ablution with clean earth (Tayammum).\n[Reported by Ad- Daraqutni in a Mawquf (untraceable) Hadith and Al-Bazzar in a Marfu' (traceable) one. Ibn Khuzaima and Al-Hakim graded it Sahih (sound)]."
"135","One of my forearms was broken. Then I consulted Allah's Messenger (Peace be upon him) and he ordered me to wipe over the bandages.\n[Reported by Ibn Majah with a very weak chain of narrators]."
"136","concerning the man who had a head injury, and then he made Ghusl and died: Allah's Messenger Peace be upon him said, \"It would have been enough for him to perform Tayammum and wrap it with something and wipe over the wrapping and wash the rest of his body.\"\n[Reported by Abu Da'ud, but there is a weakness in its chain of narrators]"
"137","It is from the Sunnah of the Prophet (ﷺ) for the man to pray only one prayer with each Tayammum, and then perform Tayammum for the next prayer.\n[Reported by Ad-Daraqutni but with a very weak chain of narrators]"
"138","Fatima bint Abu Hubaish used to have a prolonged flow of blood (Istihadah) and so Allah’s Messenger (Peace be upon him)· told her, \"If it is the blood of menstruation it will be dark (almost black) and recognizable (by women). If it is that, then leave the prayer. If it is other than that, then make ablution and pray.\"\n[Reported by Abu Da'ud and An-Nasa’i. Ibn Hibban and Al-Hakim graded it Sahih (sound).]"
"139",") \"She should sit in a tub, and if she sees yellowness appearing (on top of the water) she should wash (three times), once for the Dhuhr and Asr prayers, and once for the Maghrib and Isha prayers, and once for the Fajr prayer, and she should then perform ablution in between those times.\""
"140","'I had a very strong prolonged flow of blood. I went to the Prophet (Peace be upon him) to ask him about it. He said, \"This is a strike from Satan. So observe your menses for six or seven days, then perform Ghusl until you see that you are clean. Pray for twenty-four or twenty-three nights and days and fast, and that will suffice you. Do so every month just as the other women menstruate (and are purified). But if you are strong enough to delay the Dhuhr prayer and advance the Asr prayer, then make Ghusl when your purified and combine the Dhuhr and the Asr prayers together; then delay the Maghrib prayer and advance the Isha prayer, and perform Ghusl and combine the two prayers, do so. Do so, and then wash at dawn and pray Fajr. This is how you may pray and fast if you have the ability to do so.\" And he said, \"That is the more preferable way to me.\"\n[Reported by the five imams except An- Nasa’i, At-Tirmidhi graded it Sahih (sound)]"
"141","Umm Habiba bint Jahsh complained to Allah's Messenger (Peace be upon him) about a prolonged flow of blood. He said to her, \"Keep away (from prayer) as long as your normal period used to prevent you (from praying), and afterwards she should perform Ghusl (and pray)\". (She used to take a bath for every prayer).\n[Reported by Muslim.]"
"142","\"And perform ablution for every Salat (prayer)\". Abu Dawud and others transmitted a similar narration."
"143","After we were pure, we did not consider the yellow or muddy discharge to be anything (i.e. of the menses blood)\n[Reported by Al-Bukhari and Abu Dawud and the wording is of Abu Dawud]."
"144","The Jews used not to eat with a woman during her menstruation period, so the Prophet (Peace be upon him) said: \"Do every thing else apart from sexual intercourse (with your wives)\".\n[Reported by Muslim.]"
"145","When I was menstruating, the Prophet saws would order me to wrap myself up (with an Izar, which is a dress worn below the waist) and would start fondling me.\nReported by Al-Bukhari and Muslim."
"146","Allah's Messenger (Peace be upon him) said regarding a husband who has sexual intercourse with his wife during her menstruation period, \"He must pay a Dinar or half a Dinar in way of charity.”\n[Reported by the five Imams. Al-Hakim and Ibn Al-Qattan graded it Sahih (sound).]"
"147","Allah's Messenger (Peace be upon him) said: \"Is it not the case that when a woman menstruates, she neither prays nor fasts?\"[12]\n[Reported by Al-Bukhari and Muslim. It is part of a long Hadith]"
"148","When we came to a place called Sarif, I menstruated and the Prophet (Peace be upon him) told me, \"You should perform all that a pilgrim would do, except circumambulation until you are pure (i.e. performed Ghusl).\"\n[Reported by Al-Bukhari and Muslim and it is part of a long Hadith.]"
"149","He asked the Prophet (Peace be upon him), “What is lawful for a man regarding his wife when she is menstruating?\" and he replied, \"What is above the waist wrapper (Izar).”[13]\n[Reported by Abu Da'ud and graded it Da'if.]"
"150","During the lifetime of the Prophet (Peace be upon him) the women having bleeding after delivery (postnatal or puerperal blood) would refrain (from prayer) for forty days.\n[Reported by Al-Khamsa except An-Nasa’i, and the version is that of Abu Da’ud]."
"151","It was narrated from Hazrat Abdullah bin Umar and Hazrat Aisha that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Surely, Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) calls the call to prayer at night. You people eat and drink until the call to prayer of Ibn Umm Maktoum (RA).\" Hadhrat Ibn Umm Maktoum (RA) was a blind man, he would not call the call to prayer until people told him that it was dawn. (Bukhari and Muslim - there is a word written at the end of it.)"
"152","It was narrated on the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Umar that (one day) Hazrat Bilal recited the Adhan before dawn, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to go again and proclaim: “Beware! Indeed, the servant had fallen asleep."
"153","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"When you hear the call to prayer, say it in the same way as the muezzin is saying it.\" (Bukhari and Muslim). And Muslim narrated a hadith from Hazrat Umar, which is about the virtue of saying one word in the same way in response to the muezzin, except for haiyy ali salaat and haiyy ali al-falah, that instead of these words, say la hawla wa quwa illa bilallah."
"154","On the authority of Hazrat Uthman bin Abi Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: O Messenger of Allah! Appoint me as the Imam of my people. He said: \"You are their imam. Make the weakest among them your example and appoint a muezzin who does not take a wage for calling the call to prayer.\""
"155","Hazrat Malik bin Hawairat (RA) narrated that the Prophet (PBUH) said to us: \"When the time for prayer comes, one of you should call the Adhan for you.\" Then he narrated the entire hadith. (It has been narrated by all seven)."
"156","It is narrated from Hazrat Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Hazrat Bilal, may Allah be pleased with him: \"When you say the adhan, say it slowly, and when you say the takbeer, say it quickly.\" Leave enough time between the Adhan and the Iqamah that the person eating is finished with his food (so that he can participate in the congregation).” Then he narrated the entire hadith. (Tirmidhi narrated it and declared it weak.) And in Tirmidhi it was narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No one should say the Adhan except a person who is ablution.” It has been declared as weak.) And in the narration of Hazrat Abdullah Bin Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu in Abu Dawud, it is said that I saw it in a dream, meaning the call to prayer, and I wished to be appointed as a muezzin. He said: \"You say Takbeer.\""
"157","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"The muezzin has more right to call the call to prayer and the imam has more right to say Takbeer.\""
"158","On the authority of Hazrat Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"The prayer is not rejected in the interval between the Adhan and Iqamah.\""
"159","On the authority of Hazrat Jabir, the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever makes this supplication after hearing the Adhan, my intercession will be necessary for him on the Day of Resurrection: O Lord of this perfect supplication and everlasting prayer! Grant Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) means and virtue and grant him the position of Mahmud that You have promised him.” (Narrated by all four)."
"160","On the authority of Hazrat Ali bin Talaq, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"During the prayer, when one of you passes out, he should go back, perform ablution again, and perform the prayer again.\""
"161","Hazrat Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: “Allah does not accept the prayer of an adult woman without a turban."
"162","Hazrat Jabir (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said to him: \"When the cloth is large and loose, wrap it around the body in prayer.\" And in the tradition of Muslim, it is: \"(If the cloth is wide) put the two edges of the cloth on opposite shoulders.\" And if the cloth is tight, tie it in the form of an apron.\" (Bukhari and Muslim) And in Bukhari and Muslim it was narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira that \"None of you should pray in a cloth (in such a way) that no part of that cloth is on his shoulder.\""
"163","Hazrat Umm Salama (RA) narrated that I asked the Prophet (PBUH): Can a woman pray in just a shirt and a veil without an apron? He said: \"When the shirt is so long and loose that it reaches the upper parts of the feet, it is permissible.\""
"164","Hazrat Aamir bin Rabi'ah (RA) narrates that we were with the Prophet (PBUH) on a dark night and it became difficult for us to identify the direction of the qiblah. We prayed (by determining the direction of Qibla). When the sun rose, it became known that we had prayed towards the non-qibla, so (on that occasion) this verse was revealed: ﴾Fainama tuwalwa fatham wajhu Allah﴾ So wherever you turn, that is the face of Allah."
"165","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"The Qiblah is between the East and the West.\""
"166","Hazrat Aamir bin Rabi'ah (RA) says: \"I saw the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) praying on his camel, wherever it would lead him.\" (Bukhari and Muslim) and Bukhari has also quoted this addition that he used to point his blessed head (in prayer) and did not do so in the obligatory prayer. And it was narrated in Abu Dawud on the authority of Hazrat Anas (RA) that when he was traveling and wanted to perform the Naful prayer, he would (once) turn his camel towards the Qiblah and say Takbeer. (The chain of this hadith is Hasan)."
"167","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"The whole land is a mosque except for the graveyard and the bath.\" (Pray wherever you want)."
"168","Hazrat Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) forbade praying in seven places: Ghare (garbage), slaughterhouses, graveyards, public streets, baths, enclosures (camel tying places) and on the roof of Baitullah. (It was narrated by Tirmidhi and called it weak.)"
"169","Hazrat Abu Murshad Ghanwi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: “Neither pray facing the graves nor sit on them.” (Narrated by Muslim)."
"170","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When one of you comes to the mosque, he should look at (his shoes) (before entering the mosque). If there is any dirt or unclean thing in the shoes, then he should clean them and pray in them."
"171","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “When one of you treads dirt with his socks, the soil will purify him.”"
"172","Hazrat Mu'awiya bin Huqam (RA) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \"Indeed, there is no room for human conversation in prayer.\" In prayer, there should be only Tasbih (Glory be to Allah), Takbeer (Allahu Akbar) and recitation of the Qur’an.” (Narrated by Muslim)."
"173","Hazrat Zayd bin Arqam, may God be pleased with him, narrates that during the blessed era of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, we used to talk to each other during prayer and explain our needs and wants to each other until this verse was revealed: Protect the prayers and especially the middle prayer (Asr). And stand in silence in front of Allah.\" So we were ordered to remain silent and forbidden to talk and speak in prayer. (Bukhari and Muslim - these words are from Muslim)."
"174","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “For men, it is tasbih (informing the imam in prayer by saying Subhaan Allah) and for women, clapping their hands.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"175","Hazrat Mutaraf, may God have mercy on him, narrates from his father, Abdullah bin Shukhair, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying. (It has been narrated by all five except Ibn Majah, and Ibn Hibban has declared it Sahih.)"
"176","It was narrated from Hazrat Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) that I had two occasions to attend the service of the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him). When I was in your service and you were praying, you would call to inform me. (Narrated by Nisai and Ibn Majah.)"
"177","Hazrat Ibn Umar Radiyallahu Anhu narrates that I asked Hazrat Bilal Radiyallahu Anhu: How did you see the Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) replying when he was praying and people greeted him? He said you would do it like this. And stretched out his hand. (Narrated by Abu Dawud and Tirmidhi, and Tirmidhi declared it Sahih.)"
"178","It was narrated on the authority of Hazrat Abu Qatadah that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to carry (his granddaughter) Imama bint Zaynab while leading the prayer. When you went into prostration, you used to put it down, and when you stood up after prostrating, you would pick it up (again). (Bukhari and Muslim) and there is this addition in Muslim: You used to lead the people in the mosque."
"179","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Kill two black animals in prayer: a snake and a scorpion.\""
